# gitleaks ignore list for AA-Partner (AA-981 follow-up): one finding fingerprint per line, for a single known false
# positive that a narrow allowlist entry in .gitleaks.toml cannot express. Read by .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml
# and secret-scan-history.yml.
#
# Fingerprint formats (printed by gitleaks with --redact, never the value itself):
#   <commit sha>:<file>:<rule id>:<line>   pinned: that finding in that one commit only. Use this format.
#   <file>:<rule id>:<line>                global: that file, rule and line in EVERY commit. gitleaks 8.30 honours it
#                                          in git mode too, so it suppresses the PR job and the full-history job
#                                          for any later commit, a real secret at the same place included. Avoid
#                                          it; if one is unavoidable, put it in its own block with a comment why.
#   <blob id>/<file>:<rule id>:<line>      a UTF-16 file (the transcoded pass): that finding in that one file
#                                          content only (blob id = git hash-object of the UTF-16 file).
# Squash merges: a pinned fingerprint names one commit, and the squash merge writes the same line in a new commit on
# main. The PR check also scans a squash preview (the PR merged into the base), which a pin of a PR commit does
# not cover, so it stays red, as the full-history job would after the merge. For a false positive that a PR adds, use
# a narrow allowlist entry (regex or path) in .gitleaks.toml: it matches every commit. Pins are for findings already
# in history (old commits, squash commits on the default branch, closed PR heads).
# An inline gitleaks:allow comment on the line also survives the squash, but it hides that line from both jobs, so
# the PR job treats it like a change to this file (label needed).
# Add a short comment above each entry: what the value is and why it is not a secret. Never write the value here.
# A real secret is never ignored here: remove it, rotate it, then pin the old commit.
# A change to this file needs the PR label `secret-scan-baseline-reviewed` (see the workflow header).

# --- Full-history baseline (AA-981 follow-up, S248): the first full-history scan with .gitleaks.toml (branches,
# tags and pull request heads) found nothing, so there is no entry yet.

